    <h2 style="color:var(--primary);margin-top:40px">What is robotic knee replacement?</h2>
    <p><strong>Robotic knee replacement</strong> is a knee replacement surgery in which a computer-guided robotic arm helps the surgeon plan and execute bone cuts with sub-millimetre precision. The surgeon remains fully in control &mdash; the robot adds a real-time, computer-verified surgical plan and an instrument that cuts within a tightly controlled boundary. Robotic-assisted technique aims to improve implant alignment, ligament balance, and long-term implant survival compared with the manual jig-based technique used in conventional knee replacement.</p>
    <p>At DHS Multispecialty Hospital we perform robotic knee replacement on the <strong>VELYS Robotic-Assisted Solution</strong> from Johnson &amp; Johnson DePuy Synthes &mdash; an imageless platform that does not require a pre-operative CT scan and is paired with the globally proven J&amp;J Attune knee implant.</p>

    <h2 style="color:var(--primary);margin-top:30px">How robotic knee replacement works at DHS</h2>
    <ol style="margin:10px 0 18px 24px;line-height:1.85">
      <li><strong>Consultation &amp; imaging.</strong> Standing X-ray (and sometimes MRI), clinical examination, and review of medical conditions by Dr. Hardik Shah or Dr. Swagat Shah. No pre-op CT scan needed.</li>
      <li><strong>Pre-anaesthesia work-up.</strong> Cardiology / anaesthesia clearance, blood investigations, and an in-house physiotherapy briefing.</li>
      <li><strong>Surgery (60&ndash;90 minutes per knee).</strong> Spinal or general anaesthesia. Tracking arrays placed on the femur and tibia. Specialised probes register your knee's bone landmarks and ligament tension intra-operatively. The robotic arm then guides bone cuts within sub-millimetre tolerance, and the surgeon places the J&amp;J Attune implant.</li>
      <li><strong>Day 0.</strong> Standing and walking aided within a few hours of surgery. Pain managed with a multimodal protocol.</li>
      <li><strong>Days 2&ndash;3.</strong> Hospital discharge once you are walking comfortably with support and physiotherapy is established.</li>
      <li><strong>Weeks 1&ndash;6.</strong> Structured physiotherapy programme; gradual return to walking without aids, then driving and daily activities.</li>
      <li><strong>Months 3&ndash;4.</strong> Full recovery with complete range of motion.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 style="color:var(--primary);margin-top:30px">Who is a candidate for robotic knee replacement in Ahmedabad?</h2>
    <p>Robotic knee replacement is suitable for most patients who would otherwise need conventional knee replacement &mdash; particularly:</p>
    <ul style="margin:10px 0 18px 24px;line-height:1.85">
      <li>Adults with <strong>advanced knee osteoarthritis</strong> &mdash; bone-on-bone wear, severe pain, deformity, and stiffness despite medication, physiotherapy and injections.</li>
      <li>Patients with <strong>post-traumatic knee arthritis</strong> after an old fracture or ligament injury.</li>
      <li>Patients with <strong>rheumatoid arthritis</strong> or other inflammatory arthritis affecting the knee.</li>
      <li>Patients seeking <strong>partial (uni-condylar)</strong> knee replacement when only one compartment of the knee is affected &mdash; robotic precision is particularly valuable here.</li>
      <li>Patients needing <strong>revision knee replacement</strong>, where precision is critical to fit a revision implant into compromised bone.</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="font-size:.95rem;color:var(--text-light)">Not every patient is a candidate. Severe medical conditions, very poor bone stock, or active infection may rule out robotic surgery. We will make the call together after a face-to-face consultation and review of your X-ray.</p>

    <h2 style="color:var(--primary);margin-top:30px">Benefits of robotic knee replacement over conventional surgery</h2>
    <ul class="services-list" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr))">
      <li><strong>Sub-millimetre robotic accuracy</strong> in bone cuts</li>
      <li><strong>Real-time ligament-balance verification</strong> during surgery</li>
      <li><strong>Better implant alignment</strong> compared with manual jigs</li>
      <li><strong>Less soft-tissue trauma</strong> through more conservative cuts</li>
      <li><strong>Faster early recovery</strong> &mdash; many patients walk aided on day 0</li>
      <li><strong>No pre-operative CT scan</strong> on the VELYS platform &mdash; zero extra radiation</li>
      <li><strong>Designed for the proven J&amp;J Attune implant</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Cashless treatment</strong> with major insurers and TPAs</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="color:var(--primary);margin-top:30px">The robotic platform we use: VELYS by J&amp;J DePuy Synthes</h2>
    <p>DHS standardised on the <strong>VELYS Robotic-Assisted Solution</strong> for robotic knee replacement in Ahmedabad. It is the fastest-growing robotic knee platform in India since its November 2022 launch. Published data on VELYS shows strong alignment accuracy compared with conventional manual technique.</p>

